  "notes": "Pressure precedence follows the portal's calcCO2corr: an in-range (700-1050 hPa) Field_BP wins, else the altitude-derived pressure. An explicit pressure_hpa is passed through the Field_BP slot, so out-of-band values fall back to the altitude pressure instead of erroring as the Rust impl's validate_pressure_hpa does; in-range values behave identically. The lone raw_co2 field maps to Vaisala_CO2_avg_corr (Rust surface; the portal always computes min/avg/max from its stored columns). No constants; one optional curve slot std_curve (portal 'Vaisala corr' standard curve, a=slope, b=intercept)."
